          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11.1 Areas of Sector and Segment of a Circle"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.423,
            0.597,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have already come across the terms",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " sector "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " segment "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "of a circle in your earlier classes. Recall that the portion (or part) of the circular region enclosed by two radii and the corresponding arc is called a",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " sector "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "of the circle and the portion (or part) of the circular region enclosed between a chord and the corresponding arc is called a",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " segment "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "of the circle. Thus, in Fig. 11.1, shaded region OAPB is a",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " sector "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "of the circle with centre",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "O. $\\angle \\mathrm{AOB}$"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "is called the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.618,
            0.383,
            0.863,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.618,
                0.383,
                0.863,
                0.559
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.702,
                0.565,
                0.796,
                0.584
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 11.1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.596,
            0.902,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "angle "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "of the sector. Note that in this figure, unshaded region OAQB is also a sector of the circle. For obvious reasons, OAPB is called the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " minor sector "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and OAQB is called the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " major sector"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". You can also see that angle of the major sector is",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 6 0 ^ { \\circ } - \\angle \\mathrm { A O B }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.68,
            0.595,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, look at Fig. 11.2 in which AB is a chord of the circle with centre O. So, shaded region APB is a segment of the circle. You can also note that unshaded region AQB is another segment of the circle formed by the chord AB. For obvious reasons, APB is called the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " minor segment "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and AQB is called the",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " major segment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.821,
            0.594,
            0.879
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Remark : When we write ‘segment’ and ‘sector "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "we will mean the ‘minor segment’ and the ‘minor sector’ respectively, unless stated otherwise.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
